---These are provided as part of the following event payloads:
---@enum EntityType
EntityType = {
    ---A LocEntity. These entities are the dynamic form of location, e.g. they animate or are a MultiLoc, etc.
    LOCATION = 0,
    ---A NPCEntity.
    NPC = 1,
    ---A PlayerEntity.
    PLAYER = 2,
    ---An ObjStackEntity.
    OBJSTACK = 3,
    ---A LocEntity. These entities are the static form of location, e.g. they are interactable but do not animate, etc.
    COMBINED_LOCATION_SECTION = 12,
}

---These are provided as part of the GameStateChanged event payload.
---@enum GameState
GameState = {
    BOOT = 0,
    INIT = 1,
    LOGINSCREEN = 10,
    LOBBY = 20,
    ACCOUNT_CREATE = 23,
    GAME = 30,
    RECONNECTING = 35,
    RECONNECTING_FULL = 36,
    SWITCH_WORLD = 37,
    LOADING = 40,
}

---The payload of the Logic event.
---@class LogicEventPayload
---@field logicTick integer (Read-only) How many logic ticks have occurred since the client was started.

---The payload of the Draw event.
---@class DrawEventPayload
---@field timeDeltaSecs number (Read-only) The time, in seconds, since the last draw event (often known as the delta).

---The payload of the OptionalDependencyChanged event.
---@class OptionalDependencyChangedEventPayload
---@field pluginIdentifier string (Read-only) The identifier name of the optional dependency plugin.
---@field enabled boolean (Read-only) Whether the optional dependency plugin is now enabled or disabled.

---The payload of the OptionalPermissionChanged event.
---@class OptionalPermissionChangedEventPayload
---@field permissionName string (Read-only) The name of the permission.
---@field enabled boolean (Read-only) Whether the permission is now enabled or disabled.

---The payload of the KeyUp event.
---@class KeyUpEventPayload
---@field gameKey GameKey (Read-only) The game key which was released.
---@field systemKey SystemKey (Read-only) The system key equivalent to `gameKey` which was released.
---@field modifiers integer (Read-only) A bitfield containing the modifier keys currently held.
---@field timestamp integer (Read-only) The time, in milliseconds, when the key was released.

---The payload of the KeyDown event.
---@class KeyDownEventPayload
---@field isRepeat boolean (Read-only) Whether the key press is a repeat or not. A value of `false` means the key has just been pressed. A value of `true` means the key was already pressed and the OS has re-sent the key event as a repeat.
---@field gameKey GameKey (Read-only) The game key which was pressed.
---@field systemKey SystemKey (Read-only) The system key equivalent to `gameKey` which was pressed.
---@field modifiers integer (Read-only) A bitfield containing the modifier keys currently held.
---@field timestamp integer (Read-only) The time, in milliseconds, when the key was first pressed, or the repeat event was sent.

---The payload of the KeyTyped event.
---@class KeyTypedEventPayload
---@field char integer (Read-only) The integer value of the character generated. This can be converted to a string value with: `local keyStr = string.char(keyTypedEvent.char)`
---@field modifiers integer (Read-only) A bitfield containing the modifier keys currently held.
---@field timestamp integer (Read-only) The time, in milliseconds, when the character was generated.

---The payload of the VarTransmit event.
---@class VarTransmitEventPayload
---@field var VarType (Read-only) The variable config that triggered the event.
---@field oldValue integer|string (Read-only) The previous value of the config. The return type is determined by the variable config.
---@field newValue integer|string (Read-only) The current value of the config. The return type is determined by the variable config.

---The payload of the ChatMessage event.
---@class ChatMessageEventPayload
---@field chatMessage string (Writeable) The message received. Can be edited freely, and will be passed to any subsequent subscribed functions.
---@field senderNameUnfiltered string (Read-only) An unfiltered version of a Player Character's name. Will be an empty string if no sender is attributed to the message.
---@field senderNameFiltered string (Read-only) A filtered version of a Player Character's name intended for display, which may be altered depending on the current language context. This string may not be unique due to any filtering performed. Will be an empty string if no sender is attributed to the message.
---@field senderNameSimple string (Read-only) A filtered version of a Player Character's name without any pre- or post-fixes. Will be an empty string if no sender is attributed to the message.
---@field chatType ChatType (Read-only) The type of chat message.
---@field timestamp integer (Read-only) The time when the message was received. Timestamp is in seconds since Unix epoch.

